   624	/// Run the center-pour crater scenario at a given PIC blend and wet cohesion, returning the
   625	/// persistence metrics. Settle → pour (carve) → long drain. The wet-sand target is that the pit
   626	/// HOLDS after the drain; the negative controls vary blend (agitation) and cohesion to prove the
   627	/// hold is effective-stress cohesion, not numerical agitation.
   628	fn run_center_pour_crater(gpu: &GpuContext, blend: f32, wet_cohesion: f32) -> CraterMetrics {
