docs/brainstorms/2026-06-16-twofield-water-incompressibility-requirements.md:133:**Takeaway for the pick:** the two real-time-credible, stable-stiff routes are (a) **compliant-constraint MPM (PB-MPM)** — same WebGPU stack, open reference code — and (b) **implicit density-invariant pressure (IISPH/DFSPH-style)** folded into our existing projection (the lead recommendation). Both confirm the reframe: do **not** chase explicit EOS stiffness.
