   171	            // spacing under compression-only λ. The SHARP exponent (n=16, vs the textbook ~4) confines
   172	            // it to genuine pairing range (r → 0): it's ~0 at rest spacing yet stronger than n=4 at
   173	            // r→0. A softer exponent has a long tail that, on a thin airborne stream (free fall, where
   174	            // s_corr is one-sided with nothing to cancel it), accumulates into lateral spread and
   175	            // disperses the column — water in flight should stay ballistic/coherent. Sharpening keeps
   176	            // dense fluid pair-stable (dam-break: no clumping) while leaving the free stream alone.
