docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:140:- **Approach:** Quadratic B-spline weights (KEEP.md §3 validated math), fixed-point `atomic<i32>` P2G scatter with documented FP_SCALE/velocity-cap headroom, per-particle affine C matrix carried and updated in G2P. Gravity on the grid, plus grid-node solid-boundary treatment against the scene SDF solids (separating/no-penetration condition on grid velocities, mirroring `src/utils/sdf.rs` conventions with a "mirrors utils::sdf" WGSL comment) — boundary handling is scoped work here, not an afterthought. No pressure yet — this unit's water is a momentum-correct splashing dust.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:143:- **Test scenarios:** free-fall matches the solver's own discrete recurrence within a documented float budget; P2G→G2P round trip conserves total mass and linear momentum exactly (fixed-point) for random particle sets; angular-momentum improvement of APIC vs PIC demonstrated on a rotating blob (discrimination gap asserted); fixed-point overflow probe at the velocity cap; particles settle on the container floor without wall penetration (grid boundary-condition gate); no NaNs across 1000 steps of a dam-break-shaped fall.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:222:- **Goal:** Demonstrate the perf thesis (no Poisson → headroom) and finish the seam: scaling to 200k, budgets vs xpbd, metrics surface, docs.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:226:- **Approach:** Scaling probe across 5k→200k on water-only and full scenes; per-pass timestamp breakdown via `profile()`; compare against the xpbd baseline (profiler-as-referee, recorded in PERF_NOTES); populate `Metrics` (drawdown time, evenness placeholders where extraction is deferred); ensure the test readback surface matches the xpbd precedent so future suites can port.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:227:- **Test scenarios:** µs/Kparticle flat within a stated factor from 40k→200k (linearity gate; the maximum acceptable degradation factor is pre-registered before the 200k run, not derived from it); dispatches/frame within the final recorded budget; full V60 scene at 200k runs ≤33 ms/frame median on the reference device (the R9 real-time gate), with the gate scene's composition pre-registered before the run — particle mix (~185–190k water + 10–15k solids per KTD-5's cost bound), grid resolution, substep count, and scene duration are fixed in the test, so the gate cannot be passed with a conveniently cheap mix; an offline grid-refinement sweep (3 resolutions, 2:1 ratio) with Richardson extrapolation/GCI on one fixed scenario — for this offline study the fine-sweep budget SCALES with grid resolution so iterative error stays subdominant to truncation error (a fixed absolute sweep count would fail the asymptotic-range check for reasons unrelated to spatial discretization; the fixed real-time budget is gated separately by U3's tolerance); extrapolated values become stored regression bands; `metrics()`/`particles()`/`profile()` complete without GPU sync (timing-based smoke); web build compiles (`wasm32` target check).
