     1	//! Twofield regression gate: pure water in the V60 cup must POOL (stay spread across the cup,
     2	//! centered, pocket-free) — NOT collapse into the corner. This is the missing gate for the
     3	//! reported WaterOnly symptom: with the two-field solver, water "compresses into the corner of
     4	//! the cup and never fills up any volume". Mirrors the web WaterOnly scene
     5	//! (`Scene::v60_pour_water_only`) at the web resolution (spacing 0.16). XPBD is unaffected.
     6	//!
     7	//! ROOT CAUSE (fixed here): the V60 cup+cone air is OPEN to the atmosphere, but the U4 pocket
     8	//! detection misread it as one enclosed bubble and the bubble constraint (λ ≈ −3000) crushed the
     9	//! standing water into a corner. Two mechanisms, both fixed in src/solvers/twofield/:
    10	//!   1. The flood-fill OUTSIDE label could not reach the cup air — the fixed 24-sweep budget was
    11	//!      far short of the V60 air path, and a 6-neighbor flood cannot squeeze the label through
    12	//!      the ~1-cell-wide cone apex hole. Fix: scene-derived flood budget (grid Manhattan
    13	//!      diameter) + seed OUTSIDE from every wall-adjacent air cell (a sub-resolution void at an
    14	//!      SDF wall is open, never trapped gas) so the flood conducts through the apex.
